{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":30000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"bb034ce38fc48ab6d82ae9ad2d522bff99dbbce7792268c97dda1c20c05e065a","packTokens":17357,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":1,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":600,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"impact","tokens":122,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"contract-locked","tokens":3569,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"data-model","tokens":387,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"repomap","tokens":59,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"spec","tokens":8895,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"cb","tokens":1915,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"critic","tokens":1756,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":5,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"plan"},"pointers":[],"system":"You plan the implementation of an approved spec in an existing .NET codebase.\n- Give at least 2 options (one marked simplest), choose one, and write a decision record of at most 5 lines (adr).\n- Split into tasks TASK-1.. in dependency order. Each task: the requirements it delivers, fileScope (exact repo paths or narrow globs it may change, no overlap between tasks), 1-2 exemplar files to imitate, plannedLoc, approach (short instructions for the implementer).\n- Build in working slices, not layers. A criterion checked through the API or a screen passes only once that route or screen is wired, so the first task that adds a route or screen also wires the app's entry (the startup file, the router, the layout), and each later task adds its logic together with its own endpoint or screen. Code a slice needs (an entity, a helper) goes into the first slice that uses it, not into a task of its own. File scopes may not overlap, so have that first task register routes by convention (file-based routes, or every class of one kind found at startup): later tasks then add only their own files.\n- List a requirement on the task after which its criteria can pass. Do not leave the wiring to a last task that then holds every criterion checked through the app: each earlier task is then checked only there, in the longest and dearest task of the run. Only where the repo's structure forces layers, give the wiring task a dependsOn on every layer it serves.\n- dependsOn: only the tasks whose code this task really needs.\n- Test projects, test files and CI config are not in any file scope: tests are written separately.\n- stubs: for every NEW public type/method/endpoint the tests will call, give a compilable stub file (full file content) whose bodies throw NotImplementedException, so tests compile before implementation. Existing APIs need no stubs. Stub paths must be inside a task's fileScope.\n- protectedPathsDeclared: list any migration, CI, build-config or package-feed file you must change (a human will see it).\n- newDependencies: any NuGet package to add (name, version, registry). Prefer none.\n\nOther code that uses the changed code (found by code search; scope it only if it really has to change):\n- App.Api/Program.cs [undefined] REQ-6 (MODIFIED) points at it\n- App.Api/AppDb.cs [undefined] REQ-6 (MODIFIED) points at it\n- App.Api/SeedData.cs [undefined] REQ-7 (MODIFIED) points at it\n- contracts/openapi.yaml [undefined] REQ-7 (MODIFIED) points at it\n- App.Tests/HealthTests.cs [undefined] REQ-9 (MODIFIED) points at it\n\nAPI CONTRACT (locked, contracts/openapi.yaml). The API and the web app are both held to this OpenAPI document: plan exactly its operations, with its paths, status codes and field names. Do not change the file and do not give a stub for it; a needed change to it is a change request.\n\nopenapi: 3.0.3\ninfo:\n  title: Hive Works Maintenance Requests API\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: Shared contract for the Hive Works maintenance web app and API.\nservers:\n  - url: /api\npaths:\n  /requests:\n    get:\n      operationId: listRequests\n      summary: List maintenance requests\n      description: Returns all requests or requests matching one supported status, newest first. Equal creation timestamps have no guaranteed relative order.\n      parameters:\n        - name: status\n          in: query\n          required: false\n          description: Optional single status filter.\n          schema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/RequestStatus'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Matching requests, newest first.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/RequestList'\n              example:\n                requests:\n                  - { id: 1, createdAt: '2026-03-18T09:00:00Z', title: Kitchen tap leaking, area: Kitchen, priority: Urgent, status: Open }\n                  - { id: 2, createdAt: '2026-03-17T09:00:00Z', title: \"Projector won't power on\", area: Meeting room, priority: Normal, status: In progress }\n                  - { id: 3, createdAt: '2026-03-16T09:00:00Z', title: Wobbly desk B-14, area: Open desk, priority: Low, status: Open }\n                  - { id: 4, createdAt: '2026-03-15T09:00:00Z', title: Hand dryer not working, area: Washroom, priority: Normal, status: Open }\n                  - { id: 5, createdAt: '2026-03-14T09:00:00Z', title: Loose floor tile by entrance, area: Reception, priority: Urgent, status: In progress }\n                  - { id: 6, createdAt: '2026-03-12T09:00:00Z', title: Fridge door seal worn, area: Kitchen, priority: Low, status: Done }\n                  - { id: 7, createdAt: '2026-03-11T09:00:00Z', title: Whiteboard rail coming loose, area: Meeting room, priority: Normal, status: Done }\n                  - { id: 8, createdAt: '2026-03-10T09:00:00Z', title: \"Monitor arm won't hold position\", area: Open desk, priority: Low, status: Open }\n                  - { id: 9, createdAt: '2026-03-09T09:00:00Z', title: Reception door closer slams, area: Reception, priority: Urgent, status: Open }\n                  - { id: 10, createdAt: '2026-03-07T09:00:00Z', title: Washroom sink draining slowly, area: Washroom, priority: Normal, status: Done }\n                  - { id: 11, createdAt: '2026-03-06T09:00:00Z', title: Ceiling light flickering, area: Meeting room, priority: Urgent, status: In progress }\n                  - { id: 12, createdAt: '2026-03-05T09:00:00Z', title: Kitchen cabinet hinge loose, area: Kitchen, priority: Low, status: Done }\n        '400':\n          description: The status filter is unsupported or malformed.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'\n              example:\n                message: Status must be Open, In progress, or Done.\n                errors:\n                  status: [Unsupported status filter.]\n        '500':\n          description: The request list could not be loaded.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'\n              example:\n                message: Could not load requests.\n    post:\n      operationId: createRequest\n      summary: Create a maintenance request\n      description: Trims title and description before validation and storage. The API assigns id, createdAt, and Open status itself; optional caller-supplied values for those system-controlled fields are ignored. A description that is absent or blank after trimming is omitted from the resource.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              $ref: '#/components/schemas/CreateRequest'\n            example:\n              title: Kitchen tap leaking\n              area: Kitchen\n              priority: Urgent\n              description: Water is pooling under the sink.\n      responses:\n        '201':\n          description: The created request with system-assigned fields.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/MaintenanceRequest'\n              example:\n                id: 13\n                createdAt: '2026-03-19T10:30:00Z'\n                title: Kitchen tap leaking\n                area: Kitchen\n                priority: Urgent\n                status: Open\n                description: Water is pooling under the sink.\n        '400':\n          description: Malformed JSON, invalid field types, missing or invalid fields, or invalid values. No request is created.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'\n              example:\n                message: Request validation failed.\n                errors:\n                  title: [Title must be 3 to 80 characters.]\n                  area: [Area is required.]\n                  description: [Description must be at most 500 characters.]\n        '500':\n          description: The request could not be created.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'\n              example:\n                message: Could not create the request.\n  /requests/{id}:\n    parameters:\n      - name: id\n        in: path\n        required: true\n        description: System-generated integer request ID.\n        schema:\n          type: integer\n          format: int64\n          minimum: 1\n    get:\n      operationId: getRequest\n      summary: Get a maintenance request\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: The matching request.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/MaintenanceRequest'\n              example:\n                id: 2\n                createdAt: '2026-03-17T09:00:00Z'\n                title: \"Projector won't power on\"\n                area: Meeting room\n                priority: Normal\n                status: In progress\n        '404':\n          description: No request has this ID.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'\n              example:\n                message: Request not found.\n        '500':\n          description: The request could not be loaded for a non-not-found reason.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'\n              example:\n                message: Could not load the request.\n  /requests/{id}/status:\n    parameters:\n      - name: id\n        in: path\n        required: true\n        description: System-generated integer request ID.\n        schema:\n          type: integer\n          format: int64\n          minimum: 1\n    patch:\n      operationId: changeRequestStatus\n      summary: Change a request's status\n      description: Only status is mutable. Allowed transitions are Open to In progress, In progress to Done, and Done to Open. Requests with immutable fields or other extra properties are rejected.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              $ref: '#/components/schemas/ChangeRequestStatus'\n            example:\n              status: Done\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: The request with its updated status.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/MaintenanceRequest'\n              example:\n                id: 2\n                createdAt: '2026-03-17T09:00:00Z'\n                title: \"Projector won't power on\"\n                area: Meeting room\n                priority: Normal\n                status: Done\n        '400':\n          description: Unsupported status value or attempt to change an immutable field.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'\n              example:\n                message: Status must be Open, In progress, or Done; only status may be changed.\n                errors:\n                  status: [Unsupported status value.]\n        '404':\n          description: No request has this ID.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'\n              example:\n                message: Request not found.\n        '409':\n          description: The requested status transition is not allowed from the current status.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'\n              example:\n                message: This status transition is not allowed.\n        '500':\n          description: The status could not be updated.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse'\n              example:\n                message: Could not update the request.\ncomponents:\n  schemas:\n    RequestArea:\n      type: string\n      enum: [Kitchen, Meeting room, Open desk, Washroom, Reception]\n    RequestPriority:\n      type: string\n      enum: [Low, Normal, Urgent]\n    RequestStatus:\n      type: string\n      enum: [Open, In progress, Done]\n    MaintenanceRequest:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required: [id, createdAt, title, area, priority, status]\n      properties:\n        id:\n          type: integer\n          format: int64\n          minimum: 1\n          description: System-generated request ID.\n        createdAt:\n          type: string\n          format: date-time\n          description: System-generated UTC timestamp.\n        title:\n          type: string\n          minLength: 3\n          maxLength: 80\n        area:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/RequestArea'\n        priority:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/RequestPriority'\n        status:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/RequestStatus'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 500\n    CreateRequest:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required: [title, area, priority]\n      description: Title and description are trimmed before validation and storage. Optional id, createdAt, or status inputs are ignored and replaced by system values.\n      properties:\n        title:\n          type: string\n          minLength: 3\n          maxLength: 80\n        area:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/RequestArea'\n        priority:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/RequestPriority'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 500\n        id:\n          type: integer\n          format: int64\n          description: Optional caller-supplied value is ignored.\n        createdAt:\n          type: string\n          format: date-time\n          description: Optional caller-supplied value is ignored.\n        status:\n          allOf:\n            - $ref: '#/components/schemas/RequestStatus'\n          description: Optional caller-supplied value is ignored; created requests start Open.\n    ChangeRequestStatus:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required: [status]\n      properties:\n        status:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/RequestStatus'\n    RequestList:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required: [requests]\n      properties:\n        requests:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/MaintenanceRequest'\n    ErrorResponse:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required: [message]\n      properties:\n        message:\n          type: string\n        errors:\n          type: object\n          description: Field-keyed validation messages when applicable.\n          additionalProperties:\n            type: array\n            items:\n              type: string\n\n\nDATA MODEL. Give \"dataModel\": the tables this plan sets up or changes, as the database will hold them. A person approves it as a diagram with the plan, the factory keeps it in contracts/data-model.yaml, and after every build the database the code creates is compared with it: a missing table, a different key or a different relation fails the task.\n- Each table: name, purpose (one line), and every column with its type (string, text, int, long, decimal, bool, date, datetime, time, uuid, json, enum), required (false when it may be empty), pk on the primary-key column(s), unique where no two rows may share the value, values for an enum.\n- A relation is a foreign key: \"references\" on the column that holds it, naming the table and column it points at (a primary key or a unique column of the same type), and onDelete where it matters. A many-to-many relation is its own table with a foreign key to each side. A key over several columns together goes in the table's \"uniques\".\n- Every table has a primary key. Use the names the code will use for the tables and columns.\n- Model what is stored, not what the API returns: a field worked out on each request has no column.\n- No task writes contracts/data-model.yaml: it is the factory's file. Put the entities, the database setup and any migration in the fileScope of the first task that uses each table.\n\nRepository map:\nApp.Api/AppDb.cs\n  class AppDb\nApp.Api/Program.cs\n  class Program\nApp.Api/SeedData.cs\n  class SeedData\n    void Run(AppDb db)\nApp.Tests/HealthTests.cs\n  class HealthTests\n    Task ApiIsUp()","tools":["read_file","search","repo_map"],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"assumptions\": [\n  \"d1 ASM-1: Implement API/business-rule tests in this repository and leave the screen-flow end-to-end test to the separate web-app repository, as specified by the supplied assumption.\",\n  \"d2 ASM-1: Implement API/business-rule tests in this repository; leave the screen-flow end-to-end test to the separate web-app repository.\",\n  \"d3 ASM-1: Implement API/business-rule tests in this repository and leave the screen-flow end-to-end test to the separate web-app repository.\",\n  \"d1 ASM-2: For acceptance, “a few” sample records means at least three contract-example request rows; no exact total or status/area distribution is required, consistent with Q-1.\"\n ],\n \"critic\": [\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-1.3 and AC-1.4 require exact messages (\\\"Status must be Open, In progress, or Done.\\\", \\\"Unsupported status filter.\\\", \\\"Could not load requests.\\\") but REQ-1 cites no anchor in contracts/openapi.yaml, so nothing shows these strings come from the locked contract that Q-3 makes the only source.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"rubric\": 5,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The 500 message \\\"Could not create the request.\\\" and the rule that a description blank after trimming is left out of the response are stated with no contract anchor, although the cited CreateRequest schema only says values are trimmed before validation.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"rubric\": 5,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"REQ-4 has no anchors at all, yet it fixes the 404 message \\\"Request not found.\\\" and the 500 message \\\"Could not load the request.\\\" as contract behaviour.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-4\",\n   \"rubric\": 5,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-3.1 expects \\\"Title must be 3 to 80 characters.\\\" when the title is missing, while AC-3.2 expects the \\\"Area is required.\\\" pattern when area is missing, so missing required fields are handled inconsistently and the title case has no anchor.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"rubric\": 1,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"No AC covers a title that is all whitespace or becomes shorter than 3 characters after trimming, even though the cited contract says trimming happens before validation.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"Neither REQ-4 nor REQ-5 says what happens when {id} is not an integer, is zero or is negative (400 vs 404), so the malformed-path-parameter error path is missing.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-4\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The transition rule is read-then-write with no atomicity or concurrency requirement, so two concurrent PATCHes (for example Done→Open racing Open→In progress) can both pass the transition check against a stale status.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-5\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"No precedence is defined when an unknown id comes with an invalid body (400 vs 404), or when an invalid body targets a status that would not be an allowed transition anyway (400 vs 409).\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-5\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The intent's riskTags include auth and pii, but no requirement covers authentication, authorization or 401/403 paths, and none states that the contract defines no security, so the permission paths are left unaddressed.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"REQ-7 says SeedData.Run \\\"shall add at least three\\\" rows on every call, while REQ-8 says repeated calls must not increase the row count, so the two requirements contradict each other on any call after the first.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-7\",\n   \"rubric\": 1,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"Keying \\\"exactly one row for each selected contract-example title\\\" on title means a real user request titled \\\"Kitchen tap leaking\\\" (or existing duplicates) would force the seeder to skip, merge or delete data, which conflicts with REQ-6's promise to keep existing request records.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-8\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-7.1 and AC-8.1 only cover an empty table, so seeding into an existing database that already has request rows with Seed:Demo=true is left unspecified.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-7\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"REQ-8 cites ASM-2 as a source and the spec's assumptions list \\\"d1 ASM-2\\\", but the human only accepted ASM-1, so the \\\"at least three\\\" reading of \\\"a few\\\" and the idempotency basis rest on an assumption nobody accepted.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-8\",\n   \"rubric\": 5,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"REQ-7 requires \\\"UTC creation timestamps\\\" but does not say whether seeded createdAt values keep the contract example times (2026-03-16..18) or use the current time, so the seeded order and data cannot be checked.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-7\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"REQ-9 claims seeding happens \\\"if and only if\\\" Seed:Demo is true, but its only AC tests the false/unset case; there is no AC for the true case, and \\\"support API-operation tests that arrange rows themselves\\\" cannot be observed at any public surface.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-9\",\n   \"rubric\": 3,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"Provisioning a schema on databases that EnsureCreated already initialized, with no migration-history table, effectively replaces the existing EnsureCreated startup path, which changes how the test factory and existing deployments initialize their databases without that blast radius being stated.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-6\",\n   \"rubric\": 7,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The ACs in REQ-6 assert \\\"a row for the request is present in the database\\\" and \\\"the pre-existing table and row remain present\\\", which can only be checked by inspecting the database directly, not through the API.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-6\",\n   \"rubric\": 3,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The cited lines 20-22 of Program.cs are indented inside an enclosing block that is not shown, so the claim that startup always touches PostgreSQL (and therefore fails when it is unreachable) is not fully anchored.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-10\",\n   \"rubric\": 5,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"REQ-12 and REQ-13 duplicate each other and rely only on manual ACs (\\\"a person opens the API origin\\\", \\\"a reviewer inspects\\\"), so neither can be verified automatically at a public surface.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-12\",\n   \"rubric\": 3,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"In AC-3.2, \\\"errors.area identifies the invalid or missing area\\\" gives no exact string for an out-of-enum area, and AC-3.4's \\\"contract-defined field errors where applicable\\\" is equally vague, so neither assertion can be checked precisely.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"rubric\": 3,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  }\n ],\n \"lint\": [\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L1 ids\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L2 req-ac\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L3 ears\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L4 vague\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L5 nfr\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L6 scope\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L8 anchors\",\n   \"details\": \"ok\",\n   \"passed\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"check\": \"L9 size\",\n   \"details\": \"This spec has 13 requirements, about 2 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or rejec