ponse field errors.status contains \\\"Unsupported status filter.\\\"\",\n     \"when\": \"The client calls GET /api/requests with that status filter.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The database operation for loading the request list fails after startup.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 500 and the response message is \\\"Could not load requests.\\\"\",\n     \"when\": \"A client calls GET /api/requests.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a client calls GET /api/requests, the Maintenance Requests API shall return HTTP 200 with all matching requests ordered by createdAt descending (with no required relative order for equal timestamps), HTTP 400 with the contract ErrorResponse for malformed or unsupported status filters, and HTTP 500 with message \\\"Could not load requests.\\\" for list failures.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The database is available and contains no request matching the submitted data.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 201; the returned record has a positive system-generated id, UTC createdAt, trimmed title and description, status field \\\"Open\\\", and only fields allowed by the MaintenanceRequest schema; caller-supplied system-controlled values are not used.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client posts a valid request with padded title and description and valid caller-supplied id, createdAt, and status values.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The database is available and the request body has a valid title, area, and priority.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Both response statuses are 201 and neither returned resource has a description field.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client posts a valid request once without description and once with a description t